A||||2||AkursedX||Lowered '88 Alignment Question||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||04-08-2001||09:33 PM||||Ok, 1st off, I went through the search function and I couldn't find an answer to my question.<P>So, I have just finished up re-doing my suspension on my '88GT, and I have the Fierostore's lowering springs which have dropped my car about an inch.  Now when I go to get it aligned, will there be any problems with it getting aligned since it is lowered?<BR>  And another question is, should I still use the factory specs since it's lowered?  (I have the service manual and I am taking it with me to show the mechanic the specs.)  <P>Any feedback would be appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||sjp777||04-08-2001||09:48 PM||||I have the same car with the same springs. Rear will align no problem. Front is a little trickier. With it lowered, it runs out of adjustment before it can be put exactly to specs. Not a huge deal. My car drifts just slightly to the right after a couple hundred yards without hands on the wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||04-08-2001||09:53 PM||||You shouldn't have a problem. +5 degree front caster, about 1/2 degree neg front camber and a little bit of toe-in. In the rear you'll need 1 1/2 to 2 degrees neg camber. Depending on what struts your using you may have to grind on the bottom strut mounting hole a little to get it. Dial in a little toe-in at the rear and you'll be good to go.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> ||||reg||1
